      <Graphics lineColor="000000" lineStyle="Solid" lineWidth="1.0" connectorType="Straight" />
      <Comment source="BioCyc">This enzyme catalyses the final step in the biosynthesis of L-ascorbic acid in higher plants and in nearly all higher animals with the exception of primates and some birds |CITS: [9374475]|. The enzyme is very specific for its substrate L-galactono-1,4-lactone as D-galactono-&amp;gamma;-lactone, D-gulono-&amp;gamma;-lactone, L-gulono-&amp;gamma;-lactone, D-erythronic-&amp;gamma;-lactone, D-xylonic-&amp;gamma;-lactone, L-mannono-&amp;gamma;-lactone, D-galactonate, D-glucuronate and D-gluconate are not substrates |CITS: [9374475]|. FAD, NAD+, NADP+ and O2 (cf. |FRAME: 1.3.3.12-RXN &quot;EC 1.3.3.12, L-galactonolactone oxidase&quot;|) cannot act as electron acceptor |CITS: [9374475]|.</Comment>
